Phase 2 (FullSpectrum engine emission): register the FS mixed-filament
gradient controls + region-collapse keys in PrintObject's
invalidate_state_by_config_options.

Ported from FS v0.9.9 (`ratdoux/OrcaSlicer-FullSpectrum@v0.9.9` commit
b3c41fda), `src/libslic3r/PrintObject.cpp` lines 974-986 — a new
`else if` block that gates posSlice invalidation on 8 FS keys:

  - mixed_filament_gradient_mode
  - mixed_filament_height_lower_bound
  - mixed_filament_height_upper_bound
  - mixed_filament_advanced_dithering
  - mixed_filament_component_bias_enabled
  - mixed_filament_surface_indentation
  - mixed_filament_region_collapse
  - mixed_filament_definitions

Why this matters:

Patch 0037 added the 7 dithering / mixed-filament keys to two
EXISTING invalidation blocks. But FS source introduces a SEPARATE
`else if` block at line 974 specifically for the gradient controls.
Without that block, our v2.3.2 tree drops `mixed_filament_definitions`
on the floor in `invalidate_state_by_config_options` — meaning a
user-authored change to the virtual filament rows BETWEEN slices
silently reuses the old slice state.

End user symptom: user authors a new virtual mix in the OrcaXR UI,
hits slice, sees output identical to the prior slice. They infer the
slicer is broken; actually the engine just didn't know to invalidate.

The block is structurally a standalone `else if` chain in the same
function, after the `interlocking_*` block and before
`elefant_foot_compensation`. Easy to insert without touching anything
else.

Verified compile-clean via incremental libslic3r rebuild (2/2
objects, 0 FAILED) + ./gradlew :app:assembleDebug (full APK built).

Hard dependency: patch 0027 (PrintConfig.hpp typed declarations of
these keys).

